Compare the incoming statement with every older statement. Return one entry in comparisons for each older target,
including targets that need no change. Describe whether both statements concern the same particular person,
object, event or state at the relevant time: scope is same, distinct or unresolved. Use source evidence and time.

Choose relation=no_change for compatible descriptions, including repetition, added information and more specific
descriptions of the same state. Separate things and unresolved identity also give no_change.
Choose supersedes when the evidence establishes that an earlier condition or decision ended or was replaced.
Choose contradicts when the statements cannot both describe the same state at the same time.

The changed_targets field contains only older claims needing review for that replacement or conflict; it is empty for
no_change. The comparisons field still contains every older target. Explain the decision using the evidence.
Reviewed corrections are authoritative. The application sends changes for human review.

Return a decision for each incoming claim using its listed candidate targets. Compare only those targets. An older claim can be targeted by one proposed change in this batch; other incoming claims can add compatible evidence.

Activities and plans can coexist. Treat them as replacements only when cited evidence establishes that the older activity or plan ended or was replaced. A later timestamp orders reports; replacement requires evidence of a transition.
